# Original Idea

Slack: long clawq answers go into a Slack canvas (or attached .md) with a short summary in the thread, instead of a wall of chat. Max 2026-11-05 on a 4k-char research reply: 'we probably want to like upload a md doc or something instead of putting it straight in chat'. Scopes canvases:write and files:write are already granted. Today send_file on Slack only posts a download link. Proposal: (1) agent tool slack_canvas_create(title, markdown), which creates a channel canvas, shares it and returns the link; (2) a Slack send-path overflow rule: a final reply over ~2,500 chars becomes a canvas plus its first paragraph and the link; (3) prompt guidance for research write-ups. HTML docs don't render in Slack, so they would need a host the team can reach.

